  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Mekong Architecture &#x2013; Mekong River Commission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mekong River Commission (MRC) is a treaty-based, inter-governmental river basin organisation (RBO) with a mandate to guide sustainable and equitable use of water and related resources in the Mekong River Basin.  Australia is a long-standing development partner to the MRC.

Australia provides core funding to support implementation of the Mekong River Commission (MRC) Strategic Plan (SP 2021-25) and Mekong Basin Development Strategy (BDS) 2021-30. The funds are used for national and regional activities to promote transboundary cooperation. Additionally, Australia provides technical assistance (TA) to MRC via eWater to strengthen data and information systems and via Australian Water Partnership for smaller targeted TA. Collectively, Australia&apos;s support contributes to MRC&#x2019;s five strategic outcomes and vision of an economically prosperous, socially just, environmentally sound and climate resilient Mekong River Basin.</narrative>
  </description>
